Package: open-pointcloud-studio
Version: @DEBVERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: OpenAEC Foundation <info@open-aec.com>
Section: science
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libwayland-client0, libwayland-cursor0, libwayland-egl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcb1, libxcursor1, libxi6, libvulkan1 | libegl1
Recommends: mesa-vulkan-drivers, shared-mime-info, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk | xdg-desktop-portal-backend, xdg-utils
Suggests: zenity
Homepage: https://github.com/OpenAEC-Foundation/open-pointcloud-studio
Description: viewer and editor for laser scans and point clouds
 Open Pointcloud Studio opens laser scans and other point clouds in the LAS,
 LAZ, E57, PLY, PCD, PTX and text formats, also when a survey is many
 gigabytes large. It shows scanner stations with their photos, lets you walk
 through a scene, select, delete, thin, move and scale points, measure
 distances and areas, save views with notes, and export the result as a
 point cloud or a mesh.
 .
 The package carries Open CAD Studio, the open-source CAD application, to
 show exported DXF and DWG drawings.
 .
 The application needs a Vulkan driver, or OpenGL ES 3 through EGL.
